course: dictionary
lesson: 9721
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word sun can mean different things, so read the words around it to find out which meaning you need. «Let's sit in the sun» means the light and warmth that come from the sun. «The Sun is a star at the centre of our solar system» means the star itself, which is a different thing.
explain: Sun can also be a verb, a word for an action. «Let's sun ourselves on the grass» means lie in the sunshine to get warm. Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or is it doing something? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
explain: Some sun words are phrases. «Sunrise» is when the sun first appears in the morning, and «sunburn» is red, sore skin from too much sun. The clues in a sentence tell you which meaning you need.
fact: The Sun is a star at the centre of our solar system.
fact: The Earth goes around the Sun in one year and spins once a day, which gives us day and night.
fact: Plants need sunlight to make food.
fact: «Stars have different colours: our Sun is yellow-white.»
fact: Never look straight at the sun, and wear sunscreen and a hat on hot days.
exercise: In science, the Sun is a star at the centre of our solar system. What is the Sun? | A planet with rings | A cloud of rain | *A star at the centre of our solar system | A cold wind from the north
exercise: «Let's sit in the sun.» What does sun mean here? | A shady tree | A star in the night sky | *The light and warmth that come from the sun | A hat for the beach
exercise: In «Let's sun ourselves on the grass», what kind of word is sun? | A number | *A verb | An adjective | A noun
test: «The farther a planet is from the Sun, the longer its year.» Mercury goes around in 88 days, but Neptune needs about 165 of our years. Why does Neptune take longer? | Neptune has no light | Neptune spins faster | Neptune is closer to the Sun | *Neptune is farther from the Sun
test: «Inside the Arctic Circle there is at least one day a year when the Sun does not set.» What does does not set mean? | *The sun stays in the sky all day and does not go down | The sun goes down and comes up again in the same minute | The sun is hidden by snow forever | The sun turns into a star
exam: Why must you never look straight at the sun? | It makes plants grow | It is too cold to look at | It is only a star in science books | *It can hurt your eyes
